  m_Name: Object_37
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  partName: Cylinder Head
  description: The Cylinder Head is a small, elongated metal component positioned
    at the middle-center-center of the engine, responsible for sealing the cylinders
    and directing airflow and fuel into the combustion chamber. Made of metal-mid
    material, it provides excellent strength and thermal conductivity, and its location
    allows for efficient heat transfer and engine operation. Notably, the Cylinder
    Head is designed to work in conjunction with the engine block and valves to optimize
    engine performance and efficiency.
